    "z": "f0a1b2c3d4e5f607",
    "name": "Centrifuge: subscribe and publish",
    "info": "Prerequisites: a Centrifugo v6 server on ws://localhost:8000 that lets clients subscribe and publish on the default namespace. The repository ships one: edit quickstart/centrifugo.yaml (set client.token.hmac_secret_key), then run `centrifugo --config quickstart/centrifugo.yaml`.\n\nOpen the `centrifuge server` configuration, paste the server's `client.token.hmac_secret_key` into Secret, and deploy.\n\nExpected: the `centrifuge in` node shows `subscribed`. Click the inject button: the message is published to channel `news` and arrives back through `centrifuge in` in the debug sidebar as `{\"hello\":\"world\"}` with `msg.centrifuge.event = \"publication\"`. The output of `centrifuge out` carries `msg.centrifuge = {\"action\":\"publish\",\"channel\":\"news\"}`.",
    "x": 200,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
